# Campus Events RSVP: example requests
#
# How to use:
#   - VS Code: install the "REST Client" extension, then click "Send Request"
#     above any request. (JetBrains IDEs support .http files natively.)
#   - No extension? See docs/api-reference.md for browser-console and curl versions.
#
# Set baseUrl to your Ready Vercel deployment. Use FICTIONAL names and emails only.
# Optional local work: use http://localhost:3000 after starting npm run dev.
# Event IDs 1-4 exist after running database/seed.sql.
# In the STARTER, GET /api/events and POST /api/rsvps return 501 until finished.

@baseUrl = https://YOUR-PROJECT.vercel.app

### 1. List events -> 200 { "data": [ ... ] }
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/events

### 2. One event -> 200 { "data": { ... } }
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/events/1

### 3. Malformed event ID -> 400 INVALID_EVENT_ID
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/events/abc

### 4. Event that does not exist -> 404 EVENT_NOT_FOUND
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/events/9999

### 5. Valid RSVP -> 201 (run once; running it again gives 409)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/rsvps
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "eventId": 1,
  "name": "Alex Example",
  "email": "alex@example.com"
}

### 6. Duplicate RSVP (same event + same email, different case and spaces) -> 409 DUPLICATE_RSVP
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/rsvps
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "eventId": 1,
  "name": "Alex Example",
  "email": "  ALEX@example.com  "
}

### 7. Missing email -> 400 VALIDATION_ERROR (the browser form would stop this; the API must too)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/rsvps
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "eventId": 1,
  "name": "Sam Sample"
}

### 8. Badly formatted email -> 400 VALIDATION_ERROR
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/rsvps
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "eventId": 1,
  "name": "Sam Sample",
  "email": "not-an-email"
}

### 9. eventId as a string instead of a number -> 400 VALIDATION_ERROR
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/rsvps
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "eventId": "1",
  "name": "Sam Sample",
  "email": "sam@example.com"
}

### 10. Unknown event -> 404 EVENT_NOT_FOUND
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/rsvps
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "eventId": 9999,
  "name": "Sam Sample",
  "email": "sam@example.com"
}

### 11. Malformed JSON (missing closing brace) -> 400 INVALID_JSON
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/rsvps
Content-Type: application/json

{ "eventId": 1, "name": "Sam Sample"
